# Copy to .env for local work, or set these as BUILD variables on the host
# (Coolify: Environment Variables, "Build Variable" checked). Nothing here is
# a secret.

# Absolute base URL of the deployed site, no trailing slash.
#
# It has to be a build variable, not a runtime one: `nuxt generate` bakes the
# result into static HTML, and there is no server left afterwards to fill it
# in. It feeds
#   - the canonical link and og:url of every page,
#   - og:image (a relative OG image is ignored by every social crawler),
#   - the <loc> entries of /sitemap.xml,
#   - the Sitemap: line of /robots.txt.
#
# Unset, the site still builds and renders: URLs stay relative, the sitemap is
# emitted empty with a warning, and robots.txt omits its Sitemap: line. That is
# deliberate - a made-up domain in a canonical tag is worse than a missing one,
# which is also why this line ships commented out rather than with a placeholder
# host: copying the file as-is must not put example.com into every canonical.
# NUXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-domain.example

# Only used by `pnpm export-sources`, which reads the original photographs from
# outside every repository. Not needed to build the site.
# PHOTO_SOURCE_DIR=/path/to/originals

# Only used by `pnpm encode-video`: the directory a relative `--source` is
# resolved against. Like the photographs, the source clips live outside every
# repository and are only ever read. Not needed to build the site.
# VIDEO_SOURCE_DIR=/path/to/clips
